  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"terminal#835\", \"terminal#9082\", \"terminal#20178\"], \"answer\": \"Vertical tabs (an Edge-style side tab list) is a long-standing feature request already tracked in terminal#835, and newer requests like terminal#9082 and terminal#20178 were closed as duplicates of it. It is not implemented yet. The blocker is that the WinUI TabView control only supports tabs above the content, and the team has said it isn't on their schedule but would accept a contribution. Please add your vote or use case to terminal#835 rather than opening a new ticket. In the meantime, you can give each session a clear, short title (for example, with the shell setting the window title or by renaming the tab) so the titles are easier to read in the horizontal strip. Related ideas, such as a tree view of profiles and tabs (terminal#16387), depend on vertical tabs being done first. Tab groups are not covered by these tickets.\"}",
